{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543029-how-flexible-is-curseborn-magic","id":1543029,"title":"How flexible is Curseborn Magic?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-02T15:00:01-07:00","id":1543029,"title":"How flexible is Curseborn Magic?","content":"Do Curseborn spellcasters have a have amount of flexibility? Are their powers more like M:tA Spheres or V:tM Thaumathurgy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-02T16:11:46-07:00","id":1543034,"title":"","content":"In general I think it's more like WtF gifts, 5 powers grouped together around a theme but each act independently. Sorcerers however get some added flexibility with magic as part of their family and lineage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-03T20:18:26-07:00","id":1543079,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'm hoping for something similar to Gutter Magic, it's thematic and charming (and we are not getting it for Hunter 2nd Edition so there's that). It also has a mechanical and story edge of mixing the spellcasters magical skills to their lifestyle and habits.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24424-magus-black","name":"Magus Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-03T20:21:53-07:00","id":1543080,"title":"","content":"When Chapter 4 rolls around, we'll have a proper idea of the flexibility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-11T08:11:11-07:00","id":1543581,"title":"","content":"If you've seen the Ashcan abilities are structured like:<ul><li>Dissonance<ul><li>Cost: Bleed 1 curse dice</li> <li>Attunements: Emotional, Psychic</li> <li><i>Make an attack with Empathy at Medium range.\u200b.. (Not full rule)</i></li> </ul></li> <li>Embraced by Darkness<ul><li>Cost: Hold 2 curse die</li> <li>Attunements: Ethereal, Lineage (Dead)</li> <li><i>\u200bWhen you activate this spell, become like a shadow.\u200b.. (Not full rule)\u200b</i></li> </ul></li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-11T21:27:57-07:00","id":1543607,"title":"","content":"Everyone is a spellcaster and it's more like Thaumaturgy. Each Lineage gets 3 Practices with their own purviews. Each Practice has 5 spells at the basic level. There are some unspecified amount beyond that. Sorcerers get 7 Practices for the Lineage as a whole but only 3 Practices per Family, with more being acquired later on. Each Family also has access to 3 Motifs which are unique ways their magic works differently. You might be able to cast a subset of spells as a reflexive action, or spend more to add an additional effect, or have some spells be cheaper, etc. There isn't a free form magic system in the book as that's been confirmed by the writers. There are two more systems called Cursebinding, and Rituals. We don't really know what either does or how either works but it is some sort of additional magic mechanic beyond spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27505-dragox27","name":"Dragox27","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27505_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T12:47:19-07:00","id":1544012,"title":"","content":"I am really hoping that when they eventually give Sorcerers their own book, that the magic system for them opens up. I like Ars Magica and Mage the Ascension and Mage the Awakening that gave me the freedom to do things like setup wards or else create magic items. I want to play old school John Constantine. Not &quot;So, I cast spells in the moment to do neat stuff. I am a D&amp;D wizard!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T13:02:51-07:00","id":1544016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543029-how-flexible-is-curseborn-magic?p=1544012#post1544012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am really hoping that when they eventually give Sorcerers their own book, that the magic system for them opens up. I like Ars Magica and Mage the Ascension and Mage the Awakening that gave me the freedom to do things like setup wards or else create magic items. I want to play old school John Constantine. Not &quot;So, I cast spells in the moment to do neat stuff. I am a D&amp;D wizard!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I understand, the goal of the core is to give a quickly accessible version of each Lineage, and that there will be dedicated supplements for each in the future. Don't quote me on that, though.<br /> <br /> At any rate, it's still a little early to talk spell crafting, because they may very well have practice crafting in the powers chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-16-2024, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T13:06:51-07:00","id":1544018,"title":"","content":"I get that but I am wanting them to give us the options when they get to Sorcerers. I am not saying they can do it in the corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T14:42:55-07:00","id":1544021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543029-how-flexible-is-curseborn-magic?p=1544018#post1544018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get that but I am wanting them to give us the options when they get to Sorcerers. I am not saying they can do it in the corebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>See &quot;still a little early&quot;. Powers is Thursday next week, and that's likely where we'll see how flexible it all gets for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T16:11:07-07:00","id":1544031,"title":"","content":"Tell me you did not understand what I meant in my very first sentence without TELLING me that you did not understand what I mean in my very first sentence.<br /> <br /> I do not think that the magic will be flexible in the corebook but I am <b>hoping</b> that it gets that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T07:34:40-07:00","id":1544551,"title":"","content":"Well so far things seems to be very much static for starting characters at least, you pick a spell and it does one thing, though you can spend more experience on said spell to add more effect to it later on.<br /> <br /> What i'm confused about is that some kind of family seems to specialize in magic that they actually don't seem to have access to, like the Gaki only get access to one kind of necromantic spell or the Keeper of the vine don't seem to get any access to healing spells when the narrators in the blurb about them praise their healing magic.<br /> <br /> Then there are rituals which are not locked to specific lineages or families and don't seem to have any experience cost requirement to use them, you just need to know what they are and have the correct ingredients to cast them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T07:48:15-07:00","id":1544554,"title":"","content":"Chapter 4 has rolled around. It does not appear that sorcerers have any special degree of flexibility over and above everyone else, at least not at Entanglement 1\u20134. It's possible that higher levels of Entanglement might change that; but we won't know until further books reveal more about what Entanglement 5+ is like. <br /> <br /> I'm anticipating that Curseborne will be doing something akin to Scion, with escalating levels of Entanglement resulting in &quot;phase shifts&quot; in the Accursed nature akin to the difference between Heroes (Legend 1\u20134), Demigods (Legend 5\u20138), and Gods (Legend 9+). If I'm right about this, then Entanglement 1\u20134 Sorcerers are akin to WoD &quot;hedge magicians&quot;; Entanglement 5\u20138 Sorcerers might be more akin to WoD Awakened mages; and Entanglement 9+ Sorcerers might more readily be compared to WoD Archmasters. But at this point, that's just baseless speculation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T08:59:36-07:00","id":1544562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543029-how-flexible-is-curseborn-magic?p=1544554#post1544554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chapter 4 has rolled around. It does not appear that sorcerers have any special degree of flexibility over and above everyone else, at least not at Entanglement 1\u20134. It's possible that higher levels of Entanglement might change that; but we won't know until further books reveal more about what Entanglement 5+ is like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sad on static magic only for Sorcerers in <b>Curseborne</b>.\ud83d\ude1e Will read magics chapter in coming days so may expand on my opinion more - but, for now, I just prepare <b>Mage: the Awakening</b> 2E chronicle for game that let dynamic spellcasting AND has defined setting to explore. I still backing the <b>CB</b> core to see how line will expand with 2 official adventures and Liminalities supplement - but not having higher hopes than <b>MtAw</b> already on this field.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T11:01:54-07:00","id":1544578,"title":"","content":"I'm not super disappointed about Sorcerers not working like Awakening Mages, I think it'd cause massive balance issues and if I want to play Awakening, I'll play Awakening.<br /> <br /> I'm much more bothered by how many Families seem to be described as doing things in the flavour text they have no ability to do in game. I feel like the Gaki are the absolute worst offenders here because their feeding preference, as far as I can tell, requires them to do something they are literally not game mechanically capable of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T12:59:48-07:00","id":1544583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543029-how-flexible-is-curseborn-magic?p=1544578#post1544578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not super disappointed about Sorcerers not working like Awakening Mages, I think it'd cause massive balance issues and if I want to play Awakening, I'll play Awakening.<br /> <br /> I'm much more bothered by how many Families seem to be described as doing things in the flavour text they have no ability to do in game. I feel like the Gaki are the absolute worst offenders here because their feeding preference, as far as I can tell, requires them to do something they are literally not game mechanically capable of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless i missed something which is entirely possible they seem to be pretty poor Necromancer, tho i do recall them having access to a spirituality spell that let them summon phantasms so at least they can feast on their favored meal","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T15:42:13-07:00","id":1544598,"title":"","content":"The Gaki's major Path inheritance lets them summon a mid-level phantasm that can't resist being fed on. And their secret spell is Forbidden Temptation out of Spiritualism, which invites nearby ghosts to possess you.<br /> <br /> I don't see any way for them to &quot;sense death on the wind&quot; or &quot;see the last vision of a murder victim&quot;, but then nobody else can do those either. Maybe those are rituals the Gaki know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T16:46:42-07:00","id":1544602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543029-how-flexible-is-curseborn-magic?p=1544598#post1544598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see any way for them to &quot;sense death on the wind&quot; or &quot;see the last vision of a murder victim&quot;, but then nobody else can do those either. Maybe those are rituals the Gaki know.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's an Otherworldly Sense Trick that you can purchase with hits from curse dice. It allows you to gather evidence of supernatural phenomena and it's something that any Accursed can do. What's less clear is whether this would allow a character to outright see ghosts/phantasms or similarly elusive supernatural things. I'd assume not since that seems to be what spells like Sense Hidden and Prestige are for.<br /> <br /> Unless I'm missing something though, the closest thing the Hungry have to that through their own Practices is Tenebrous Sight, which allows them to see through darkness but not through other forms of concealment.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27894-paramecius","name":"Paramecius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27894_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T17:43:03-07:00","id":1544609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543029-how-flexible-is-curseborn-magic?p=1544598#post1544598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Gaki's major Path inheritance lets them summon a mid-level phantasm that can't resist being fed on. And their secret spell is Forbidden Temptation out of Spiritualism, which invites nearby ghosts to possess you.</div> </div> </div> </div>True but what that means in practice is that if you make Gaki your Major Path you can use your limited-use Inheritance to feed once a session.<br /> <br /> Forbidden Temptation allows you to bleed 2 CD for a chance at being able to feed on a ghost to get one of them back, at the risk of being possessed or of just not actually being near any ghosts since as far as I can tell you can't see them. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't see any way for them to &quot;sense death on the wind&quot; or &quot;see the last vision of a murder victim&quot;, but then nobody else can do those either. Maybe those are rituals the Gaki know. </div> </div> </div>If they are, they're not in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28625,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","user":"Nobody Special","date":". 10-23-2024, 09:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}